  "id": "pr-262",
  "instruction": "Update `glom.cli` so users can run glom transformations from the console against target data supplied as a command-line value, a file, or standard input. Target input must support JSON, YAML, TOML, and Python-literal data, with an explicit or otherwise unambiguous way to select the format; YAML targets must work through the CLI’s main entry point. The transformation/specification must likewise be usable from the command line or an input source and must be applied to the decoded target using the normal glom semantics, with the resulting value emitted in a useful serialized form. Preserve the existing CLI usage where practical, and provide clear command-line errors and nonzero failure status for missing input, unsupported formats, malformed data/specifications, or transformation failures. Python data parsing must not execute arbitrary code merely because it is supplied as target input; only safe literal data should be accepted. Ensure the CLI and its test tooling operate correctly on Python 3.10, including tox configuration and any compatibility issues. Success is demonstrated by invoking the main CLI entry point with a YAML target and obtaining the expected glom result, while equivalent JSON, TOML, Python, file, argument, and stdin inputs behave consistently and unsafe Python expressions are rejected.",
